; Alice pays, then Bob leaks; flag stays false. A branch of OR that is a
; prohibition completes at once, so a reading has reached a prohibition and the
; term is watched to the end of the trace, whatever the other branch does:
; "alice MUST pay THEN (bob MUST_NOT leak OR alice MAY ship)" and
; "alice MUST pay OR bob MUST_NOT leak" are VIOLATED at the leak, entry 2, like
; "bob MUST_NOT leak OR alice MAY ship" alone (the conservative reading of OR,
; formal/core/CORE.md, decision 34). The first term is violated at entry 2 as
; in sequence_prohibition_violated. In the second term the guard never fires,
; the handler is never reached, and the payment completes the term at entry 1.
(scenario readings_or_pay_leak
  (spec "examples/core/core_readings.triel")
  (entry "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z" (activate)
    (data (flag (bool false))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T01:00:00Z" (act alice pay must)
    (data (flag (bool false))))
  (entry "2026-06-01T02:00:00Z" (act bob leak must_not)
    (data (flag (bool false)))))
